{"Updating the database within a validation check is a side effect that can lead to inconsistent data, as validations are often called multiple times or in contexts where persistent changes are not expected": 0.8790708184242249, "The regular expression is not anchored to the end of the string, allowing potential bypasses where emails like user@gmail.com.attacker.com would incorrectly match whitelisted domains - should use $ anchor": 0.7430651187896729, "Use find_by(email: email) instead of where(email: email).first for better readability and idiomatic Rails": 0.13564157485961914, "Use && instead of and for boolean logic in control structures due to higher precedence and Ruby standards": 0.3140121102333069, "Client-side logic adds email to rejectedEmails for any server-side error including 'email already taken', causing generic 'invalid' messages to mask the actual error reason - should only add to rejectedEmails for specifically blocked/restricted email errors": 0.8042752146720886}